{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787507894772,"sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"read:11","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T5-review-queue/prompt.md"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T5-review-queue/prompt.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Cross-layer feature: build a run review queue\n2: \n3: Complete the dependency-free run review queue in\n4: `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue`. The feature spans an in-memory store, a\n5: JSON-style API boundary, a server-rendered HTML page, tests, and operator\n6: documentation.\n7: \n8: Implement only these files:\n9: \n10: - `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-store.mjs`\n11: - `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-api.mjs`\n12: - `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-page.mjs`\n13: - `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs`\n14: - `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md`\n15: \n16: Do not edit the committed `review-queue.test.mjs` suite.\n17: \n18: ## In-memory store\n19: \n20: Export `createReviewStore({ now } = {})` from `review-store.mjs`.\n21: \n22: - `now` defaults to a function returning the current ISO timestamp. Reject a\n23:   non-function `now` with `TypeError`; each returned timestamp must be a\n24:   non-empty string.\n25: - Keep at most one current review per `runId`.\n26: - Expose `save(review)`, `get(runId)`, and `list({ decision } = {})`.\n27: - A saved input has string fields `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`.\n28:   Reject a non-object input or a non-string field with `TypeError`.\n29: - `save` calls `now` once. A new run uses that value for both `createdAt` and\n30:   `updatedAt`. An update preserves `createdAt` and replaces `updatedAt`.\n31: - `save` returns `{ created, review }`, where `created` distinguishes insert\n32:   from update. `get` returns a review or `null`.\n33: - `list` optionally filters by exact decision. Sort newest `updatedAt` first,\n34:   then lexicographically smaller `runId` for a timestamp tie.\n35: - Returned objects and arrays must be copies. A caller must not be able to\n36:   mutate stored state through a returned value.\n37: \n38: ## API boundary\n39: \n40: Export `createReviewApi(store)` from `review-api.mjs`. Reject a store without\n41: `save`, `get`, and `list` functions with `TypeError`. Return a synchronous\n42: `handleReviewRequest(request)` function.\n43: \n44: Every response has exactly the shape `{ status, headers, body }` and includes\n45: the header `content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n46: \n47: ### `POST /api/reviews`\n48: \n49: - Accept only `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`; report sorted unknown\n50:   field names as a `body` field error.\n51: - Trim all four string values before validation and storage.\n52: - `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n53: - `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n54: - `reviewer` must contain 2 through 40 characters after trimming.\n55: - `note` is at most 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n56:   `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n57: - Report all detected field problems with status 400 and\n58:   `{ error: \"validation_failed\", fields: { ... } }`. Do not save invalid data.\n59: - Return `{ review }` with status 201 for a new run and 200 for an update.\n60: \n61: ### Reads and errors\n62: \n63: - `GET /api/reviews` returns `{ reviews, summary }`. `summary` always counts all\n64:   stored reviews and has exactly `total`, `approve`, `reject`, and\n65:   `needs-work`. An optional `decision` query filters only `reviews`; an invalid\n66:   decision returns the standard validation error.\n67: - `GET /api/reviews/:runId` returns `{ review }` or status 404 with\n68:   `{ error: \"review_not_found\" }`.\n69: - Unsupported methods on a recognized route return status 405 with\n70:   `{ error: \"method_not_allowed\" }` and an `allow` header (`GET, POST` for the\n71:   collection and `GET` for a detail route).\n72: - Unknown routes return status 404 with `{ error: \"not_found\" }`.\n73: - An unusable request object or URL returns status 400 with\n74:   `{ error: \"invalid_request\" }` rather than throwing.\n75: \n76: ## User-facing page\n77: \n78: Export `renderReviewPage({ reviews, summary, message = \"\" })` from\n79: `review-page.mjs` and return a complete HTML document.\n80: \n81: - Include one main heading, a short explanation, and a `main` landmark.\n82: - Show all four summary values.\n83: - Include a POST form for the four review fields. Every control must have a\n84:   matching `label`; describe when the note is required.\n85: - Put `message` in a polite live status region.\n86: - Render reviews in a table with a caption and column headers. Show run ID,\n87:   decision, reviewer, note, and updated timestamp. Render `No reviews yet.` as\n88:   the empty state.\n89: - HTML-escape every dynamic value, including message, summary values, and all\n90:   review fields. Do not allow caller data to create tags or attributes.\n91: \n92: ## Tests and documentation\n93: \n94: - Add at least three meaningful `node:test` cases to `student-tests.mjs`. Do not\n95:   use skips, todos, or placeholder assertions.\n96: - Update `README.md` with the three routes, input and error behavior, and the\n97:   fact that the store resets on process restart because it is not durable.\n98: \n99: Run:\n100: \n101: `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs`\n102: \n103: In the final response, summarize the design, tests added, verification result,\n104: and any remaining concern.\n\n(End of file - total 104 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Cross-layer feature: build a run review queue\n\nComplete the dependency-free run review queue in\n`benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue`. The feature spans an in-memory store, a\nJSON-style API boundary, a server-rendered HTML page, tests, and operator\ndocumentation.\n\nImplement only these files:\n\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-store.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-api.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-page.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md`\n\nDo not edit the committed `review-queue.test.mjs` suite.\n\n## In-memory store\n\nExport `createReviewStore({ now } = {})` from `review-store.mjs`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T5-review-queue/prompt.md","text":"# Cross-layer feature: build a run review queue\n\nComplete the dependency-free run review queue in\n`benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue`. The feature spans an in-memory store, a\nJSON-style API boundary, a server-rendered HTML page, tests, and operator\ndocumentation.\n\nImplement only these files:\n\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-store.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-api.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-page.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs`\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md`\n\nDo not edit the committed `review-queue.test.mjs` suite.\n\n## In-memory store\n\nExport `createReviewStore({ now } = {})` from `review-store.mjs`.\n\n- `now` defaults to a function returning the current ISO timestamp. Reject a\n  non-function `now` with `TypeError`; each returned timestamp must be a\n  non-empty string.\n- Keep at most one current review per `runId`.\n- Expose `save(review)`, `get(runId)`, and `list({ decision } = {})`.\n- A saved input has string fields `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`.\n  Reject a non-object input or a non-string field with `TypeError`.\n- `save` calls `now` once. A new run uses that value for both `createdAt` and\n  `updatedAt`. An update preserves `createdAt` and replaces `updatedAt`.\n- `save` returns `{ created, review }`, where `created` distinguishes insert\n  from update. `get` returns a review or `null`.\n- `list` optionally filters by exact decision. Sort newest `updatedAt` first,\n  then lexicographically smaller `runId` for a timestamp tie.\n- Returned objects and arrays must be copies. A caller must not be able to\n  mutate stored state through a returned value.\n\n## API boundary\n\nExport `createReviewApi(store)` from `review-api.mjs`. Reject a store without\n`save`, `get`, and `list` functions with `TypeError`. Return a synchronous\n`handleReviewRequest(request)` function.\n\nEvery response has exactly the shape `{ status, headers, body }` and includes\nthe header `content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n\n### `POST /api/reviews`\n\n- Accept only `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`; report sorted unknown\n  field names as a `body` field error.\n- Trim all four string values before validation and storage.\n- `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n- `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n- `reviewer` must contain 2 through 40 characters after trimming.\n- `note` is at most 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n  `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n- Report all detected field problems with status 400 and\n  `{ error: \"validation_failed\", fields: { ... } }`. Do not save invalid data.\n- Return `{ review }` with status 201 for a new run and 200 for an update.\n\n### Reads and errors\n\n- `GET /api/reviews` returns `{ reviews, summary }`. `summary` always counts all\n  stored reviews and has exactly `total`, `approve`, `reject`, and\n  `needs-work`. An optional `decision` query filters only `reviews`; an invalid\n  decision returns the standard validation error.\n- `GET /api/reviews/:runId` returns `{ review }` or status 404 with\n  `{ error: \"review_not_found\" }`.\n- Unsupported methods on a recognized route return status 405 with\n  `{ error: \"method_not_allowed\" }` and an `allow` header (`GET, POST` for the\n  collection and `GET` for a detail route).\n- Unknown routes return status 404 with `{ error: \"not_found\" }`.\n- An unusable request object or URL returns status 400 with\n  `{ error: \"invalid_request\" }` rather than throwing.\n\n## User-facing page\n\nExport `renderReviewPage({ reviews, summary, message = \"\" })` from\n`review-page.mjs` and return a complete HTML document.\n\n- Include one main heading, a short explanation, and a `main` landmark.\n- Show all four summary values.\n- Include a POST form for the four review fields. Every control must have a\n  matching `label`; describe when the note is required.\n- Put `message` in a polite live status region.\n- Render reviews in a table with a caption and column headers. Show run ID,\n  decision, reviewer, note, and updated timestamp. Render `No reviews yet.` as\n  the empty state.\n- HTML-escape every dynamic value, including message, summary values, and all\n  review fields. Do not allow caller data to create tags or attributes.\n\n## Tests and documentation\n\n- Add at least three meaningful `node:test` cases to `student-tests.mjs`. Do not\n  use skips, todos, or placeholder assertions.\n- Update `README.md` with the three routes, input and error behavior, and the\n  fact that the store resets on process restart because it is not durable.\n\nRun:\n\n`node --test benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs`\n\nIn the final response, summarize the design, tests added, verification result,\nand any remaining concern.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":104,"totalLines":104,"truncated":false}},"title":"benchmark/tasks/T5-review-queue/prompt.md","time":{"start":1787507894766,"end":1787507894770}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have all the info I need. Let me also check the prompt.md in the task directory, which is presumably the same as the task in the user's message.\n\nLet me check quickly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_02fc5e9ea001NFYjYHCsF1GW4a","sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","messageID":"msg_02fc5e28b001XYJofGi5mhQ7xZ"}}
