{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787507967507,"sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"write:14","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-store.mjs","content":"const REVIEW_FIELDS = [\"runId\", \"decision\", \"reviewer\", \"note\"];\n\nfunction defaultNow() {\n  return new Date().toISOString();\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction copyReview(review) {\n  return {\n    runId: review.runId,\n    decision: review.decision,\n    reviewer: review.reviewer,\n    note: review.note,\n    createdAt: review.createdAt,\n    updatedAt: review.updatedAt,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction compareReviews(a, b) {\n  if (a.updatedAt > b.updatedAt) {\n    return -1;\n  }\n  if (a.updatedAt < b.updatedAt) {\n    return 1;\n  }\n  if (a.runId < b.runId) {\n    return -1;\n  }\n  if (a.runId > b.runId) {\n    return 1;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\nexport function createReviewStore({ now } = {}) {\n  const clock = now === undefined ? defaultNow : now;\n  if (typeof clock !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"createReviewStore: now must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const reviews = new Map();\n\n  function save(input) {\n    if (!isRecord(input)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"save: review must be an object\");\n    }\n    for (const field of REVIEW_FIELDS) {\n      if (typeof input[field] !== \"string\") {\n        throw new TypeError(`save: review.${field} must be a string`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    const timestamp = clock();\n    if (typeof timestamp !== \"string\" || timestamp.length === 0) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"save: now must return a non-empty string\");\n    }\n\n    const existing = reviews.get(input.runId);\n    const created = existing === undefined;\n    const stored = {\n      runId: input.runId,\n      decision: input.decision,\n      reviewer: input.reviewer,\n      note: input.note,\n      createdAt: created ? timestamp : existing.createdAt,\n      updatedAt: timestamp,\n    };\n    reviews.set(input.runId, stored);\n\n    return { created, review: copyReview(stored) };\n  }\n\n  function get(runId) {\n    const stored = reviews.get(runId);\n    return stored === undefined ? null : copyReview(stored);\n  }\n\n  function list({ decision } = {}) {\n    const selected = [];\n    for (const review of reviews.values()) {\n      if (decision === undefined || review.decision === decision) {\n        selected.push(copyReview(review));\n      }\n    }\n    selected.sort(compareReviews);\n    return selected;\n  }\n\n  return { save, get, list };\n}\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-store.mjs","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-store.mjs","time":{"start":1787507967489,"end":1787507967504}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting — the bash tool is restricted to only the exact verification command: `node --test benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs`. So I can't run `git status`, `node --version`, or any other shell command. That's fine — I'll write the code carefully and only run the allowed test command at the end.\n\nI already read package.json? No — that was blocked. Fine, I don't strictly need it. I'll write modern but conservative ESM JavaScript (the fixture files are .mjs and tests use node:test, so Node 18+ is guaranteed; `??` and optional chaining are fine).\n\nLet me now write the five files.\n\n1. `review-store.mjs` — as designed above.\n2. `review-api.mjs` — as designed.\n3. `review-page.mjs` — as designed.\n4. `student-tests.mjs` — four tests.\n5. `README.md` — documentation.\n\nLet me be careful with the store: reject arrays. `typeof [] === \"object\"` and Array.isArray → reject. Also reject null.\n\nOne thing to decide: in `save`, the plan says validate input fully before calling `now()`. ✓ my code does that.\n\nFor the page — careful with the regex from the visible test: `/<label for=\"run-id\">Run ID<\\/label>/`. My HTML must contain that exact substring. I'll write labels on one line each.\n\nAlso `/<main>/` — must contain literal `<main>`.\n\nLet me also think about whether `handleReviewRequest` should handle `request` being a function — `isPlainRecord` requires object non-null non-array. A function request → invalid_request. Fine.\n\nWhat about `new URL(url, \"http://localhost\")` when url contains spaces, e.g. \"/api/reviews run\"? URL constructor is lenient — it encodes spaces. Won't throw. Fine, then pathname won't match → not_found. Acceptable.\n\nWhen would URL parsing actually throw? E.g. `url = \"http://\"` (with base, absolute \"http://\" → invalid → throws) → invalid_request. Good.\n\nDetail route: `/api/reviews/run-alpha/extra` → rawId contains \"/\" → falls through to not_found. ✓\n\nEdge: `GET /api/reviews/` → strip one trailing slash → `/api/reviews` → collection. ✓\n\nEdge: `POST /api/reviews/` → collection → POST handler. ✓\n\nNow — one subtle point on `searchParams.has(\"decision\")` vs getting: `?decision=approve&decision=reject` → `get` returns the first (\"approve\"). Fine, unspecified.\n\nAnother subtlety: The `summary` should count from the unfiltered list. ✓\n\nNow write the page. Requirements recap:\n- complete HTML document (doctype, html, head, body)\n- one h1, short explanation, main landmark\n- all four summary values visible\n- POST form, four controls with matching labels, note-required description\n- message in aria-live=\"polite\" region\n- table with caption + column headers, five columns, empty state \"No reviews yet.\"\n- escape everything dynamic\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```js\nconst HTML_ESCAPES = {\n  \"&\": \"&amp;\",\n  \"<\": \"&lt;\",\n  \">\": \"&gt;\",\n  '\"': \"&quot;\",\n  \"'\": \"&#39;\",\n};\n\nfunction escapeHtml(value) {\n  return String(value).replace(/[&<>\"']/g, (character) => HTML_ESCAPES[character]);\n}\n\nfunction summaryNumber(summary, key) {\n  const value = summary[key];\n  return value === undefined || value === null ? 0 : value;\n}\n\nfunction renderSummaryList(summary) {\n  const items = [\n    [\"Total reviews\", summaryNumber(summary, \"total\")],\n    [\"Approved\", summaryNumber(summary, \"approve\")],\n    [\"Rejected\", summaryNumber(summary, \"reject\")],\n    [\"Needs work\", summaryNumber(summary, \"needs-work\")],\n  ];\n  return items\n    .map(([label, value]) => `          <li><strong>${escapeHtml(label)}:</strong> ${escapeHtml(value)}</li>`)\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\nfunction renderRows(reviews) {\n  if (reviews.length === 0) {\n    return '          <tr><td colspan=\"5\">No reviews yet.</td></tr>';\n  }\n  return reviews\n    .map((review) => {\n      const safe = review && typeof review === \"object\" ? review : {};\n      return [\n        \"          <tr>\",\n        `            <td>${escapeHtml(safe.runId ?? \"\")}</td>`,\n        `            <td>${escapeHtml(safe.decision ?? \"\")}</td>`,\n        `            <td>${escapeHtml(safe.reviewer ?? \"\")}</td>`,\n        `            <td>${escapeHtml(safe.note ?? \"\")}</td>`,\n        `            <td>${escapeHtml(safe.updatedAt ?? \"\")}</td>`,\n        \"          </tr>\",\n      ].join(\"\\n\");\n    })\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n}\n\nexport function renderReviewPage({ reviews = [], summary = {}, message = \"\" } = {}) {\n  const safeReviews = Array.isArray(reviews) ? reviews : [];\n  const safeSummary = summary && typeof summary === \"object\" ? summary : {};\n\n  return `<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <title>Run review queue</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <main>\n      <h1>Run review queue</h1>\n      <p>Review benchmark runs and record one current decision per run.</p>\n      <section aria-labelledby=\"summary-heading\">\n        <h2 id=\"summary-heading\">Queue summary</h2>\n        <ul>\n${renderSummaryList(safeSummary)}\n        </ul>\n      </section>\n      <p class=\"status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">${escapeHtml(message)}</p>\n      <section aria-labelledby=\"form-heading\">\n        <h2 id=\"form-heading\">Save a review</h2>\n        <form method=\"post\" action=\"/api/reviews\">\n          <p>\n            <label for=\"run-id\">Run ID</label>\n            <input id=\"run-id\" name=\"runId\" type=\"text\" required>\n          </p>\n          <p>\n            <label for=\"decision\">Decision</label>\n            <select id=\"decision\" name=\"decision\">\n              <option value=\"approve\">approve</option>\n              <option value=\"reject\">reject</option>\n              <option value=\"needs-work\">needs-work</option>\n            </select>\n          </p>\n          <p>\n            <label for=\"reviewer\">Reviewer</label>\n            <input id=\"reviewer\" name=\"reviewer\" type=\"text\" required>\n          </p>\n          <p>\n            <label for=\"note\">Note</label>\n            <textarea id=\"note\" name=\"note\" aria-describedby=\"note-help\"></textarea>\n          </p>\n          <p id=\"note-help\">A note is required when the decision is reject or needs-work; it is optional for approve. Notes are limited to 240 characters.</p>\n          <p>\n            <button type=\"submit\">Save review</button>\n          </p>\n        </form>\n      </section>\n      <table>\n        <caption>Saved run reviews</caption>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Run ID</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Decision</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Reviewer</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Note</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Updated</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n${renderRows(safeReviews)}\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </main>\n  </body>\n</html>`;\n}\n```\n\nCheck visible-test regexes against this:\n- `/<main>/` → `<main>` present ✓\n- `/<label for=\"run-id\">Run ID<\\/label>/` → `<label for=\"run-id\">Run ID</label>` ✓\n- `/aria-live=\"polite\"/` ✓\n- `/<caption>Saved run reviews<\\/caption>/` ✓\n- `/No reviews yet\\./` ✓ (in empty state; note also the empty state text appears only when reviews is empty — the committed test passes reviews: []) ✓\n\nAll dynamic values escaped: message ✓, summary values ✓ (labels are static), review fields ✓.\n\nNote: `??` requires Node 14+; fine. But hmm, `escapeHtml(safe.runId ?? \"\")` — if runId is a number, String(number) works. Good.\n\nOne question: form control for note — a textarea's label association works with for/id. ✓\n\nNow the API file — full code:\n\n```js\nconst CONTENT_TYPE = \"application/json; charset=utf-8\";\nconst DECISIONS = [\"approve\", \"reject\", \"needs-work\"];\nconst BODY_FIELDS = [\"runId\", \"decision\", \"reviewer\", \"note\"];\nconst RUN_ID_PATTERN = /^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$/;\nconst COLLECTION_PATH = \"/api/reviews\";\nconst DETAIL_PREFIX = \"/api/reviews/\";\nconst REVIEWER_MIN_LENGTH = 2;\nconst REVIEWER_MAX_LENGTH = 40;\nconst NOTE_MAX_LENGTH = 240;\n\nfunction respond(status, body, extraHeaders) {\n  return {\n    status,\n    headers: { \"content-type\": CONTENT_TYPE, ...extraHeaders },\n    body,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nWait — `...extraHeaders` when extraHeaders is undefined → spreading undefined in object literal is fine (`{...undefined}` → `{}`). Yes, that's valid JS.\n\n```js\nfunction validationFailed(fields) {\n  return respond(400, { error: \"validation_failed\", fields });\n}\n\nfunction invalidRequest() {\n  return respond(400, { error: \"invalid_request\" });\n}\n\nfunction methodNotAllowed(allow) {\n  return respond(405, { error: \"method_not_allowed\" }, { allow });\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction isValidDecision(value) {\n  return DECISIONS.includes(value);\n}\n\nexport function createReviewApi(store) {\n  if (\n    store === null ||\n    store === undefined ||\n    typeof store.save !== \"function\" ||\n    typeof store.get !== \"function\" ||\n    typeof store.list !== \"function\"\n  ) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"store must provide save, get, and list functions\");\n  }\n\n  function handlePost(body) {\n    if (!isRecord(body)) {\n      return validationFailed({\n        body: \"body must be an object with runId, decision, reviewer, and note\",\n      });\n    }\n\n    const fields = {};\n    const unknown = Object.keys(body)\n      .filter((key) => !BODY_FIELDS.includes(key))\n      .sort();\n    if (unknown.length > 0) {\n      fields.body = `Unknown fields: ${unknown.join(\", \")}`;\n    }\n\n    const trimmed = {};\n    for (const field of BODY_FIELDS) {\n      const value = body[field];\n      if (typeof value !== \"string\") {\n        fields[field] = `${field} must be a string`;\n      } else {\n        trimmed[field] = value.trim();\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (trimmed.runId !== undefined && !RUN_ID_PATTERN.test(trimmed.runId)) {\n      fields.runId = \"runId must match run- followed by 3-64 lowercase letters, digits, or hyphens\";\n    }\n    if (trimmed.decision !== undefined && !isValidDecision(trimmed.decision)) {\n      fields.decision = \"decision must be approve, reject, or needs-work\";\n    }\n    if (\n      trimmed.reviewer !== undefined &&\n      (trimmed.reviewer.length < REVIEWER_MIN_LENGTH || trimmed.reviewer.length > REVIEWER_MAX_LENGTH)\n    ) {\n      fields.reviewer = \"reviewer must contain 2 through 40 characters\";\n    }\n    if (trimmed.note !== undefined) {\n      if (trimmed.note.length > NOTE_MAX_LENGTH) {\n        fields.note = \"note must be at most 240 characters\";\n      } else if (\n        trimmed.note.length === 0 &&\n        (trimmed.decision === \"reject\" || trimmed.decision === \"needs-work\")\n      ) {\n        fields.note = \"note is required for reject and needs-work\";\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (Object.keys(fields).length > 0) {\n      return validationFailed(fields);\n    }\n\n    const { created, review } = store.save(trimmed);\n    return respond(created ? 201 : 200, { review });\n  }\n\n  function handleCollection(searchParams) {\n    const all = store.list();\n    const summary = { total: all.length, approve: 0, reject: 0, \"needs-work\": 0 };\n    for (const review of all) {\n      if (review.decision === \"approve\") {\n        summary.approve += 1;\n      } else if (review.decision === \"reject\") {\n        summary.reject += 1;\n      } else if (review.decision === \"needs-work\") {\n        summary[\"needs-work\"] += 1;\n      }\n    }\n\n    let reviews = all;\n    if (searchParams.has(\"decision\")) {\n      const decision = searchParams.get(\"decision\");\n      if (!isValidDecision(decision)) {\n        return validationFailed({ decision: \"decision must be approve, reject, or needs-work\" });\n      }\n      reviews = all.filter((review) => review.decision === decision);\n    }\n\n    return respond(200, { reviews, summary });\n  }\n\n  function handleDetail(runId) {\n    const review = store.get(runId);\n    if (review === null) {\n      return respond(404, { error: \"review_not_found\" });\n    }\n    return respond(200, { review });\n  }\n\n  function handleReviewRequest(request) {\n    if (!isRecord(request)) {\n      return invalidRequest();\n    }\n    const { method, url } = request;\n    if (typeof method !== \"string\" || typeof url !== \"string\" || url.length === 0) {\n      return invalidRequest();\n    }\n\n    let parsed;\n    try {\n      parsed = new URL(url, \"http://localhost\");\n    } catch {\n      return invalidRequest();\n    }\n\n    let pathname = parsed.pathname;\n    if (pathname.length > 1 && pathname.endsWith(\"/\")) {\n      pathname = pathname.slice(0, -1);\n    }\n    const upperMethod = method.toUpperCase();\n\n    if (pathname === COLLECTION_PATH) {\n      if (upperMethod === \"POST\") {\n        return handlePost(request.body);\n      }\n      if (upperMethod === \"GET\") {\n        return handleCollection(parsed.searchParams);\n      }\n      return methodNotAllowed(\"GET, POST\");\n    }\n\n    if (pathname.startsWith(DETAIL_PREFIX)) {\n      const rawId = pathname.slice(DETAIL_PREFIX.length);\n      if (rawId.length === 0 || rawId.includes(\"/\")) {\n        return respond(404, { error: \"not_found\" });\n      }\n      let runId;\n      try {\n        runId = decodeURIComponent(rawId);\n      } catch {\n        return invalidRequest();\n      }\n      if (upperMethod !== \"GET\") {\n        return methodNotAllowed(\"GET\");\n      }\n      return handleDetail(runId);\n    }\n\n    return respond(404, { error: \"not_found\" });\n  }\n\n  return handleReviewRequest;\n}\n```\n\nWait — one issue: `pathname.startsWith(DETAIL_PREFIX)` after stripping one trailing slash. `/api/reviews/run-1/` → strip trailing slash → `/api/reviews/run-1` → detail. Good.\n\n`/api/reviews//` → strip one → `/api/reviews/` → startsWith DETAIL_PREFIX, rawId = \"\" → not_found. Good.\n\nEmpty method string: `typeof method === \"string\"` passes for \"\"... `\"\".toUpperCase()` → \"\" → on collection → 405? Hmm, an empty method is \"unusable request\" arguably → invalid_request. The plan says \"must be a string; uppercase it\". An empty-string method on a recognized route → 405 seems fine; but is an empty method \"unusable\"? To be safe, treat empty method as invalid_request: `method.length === 0` → invalid_request. I'll add that check. It aligns with \"unusable request object\".\n\nHmm, but what about method \"  \" (whitespace)? Uppercase → same → 405 on known route, or 404 not_found for unknown path... method check happens per route. For unknown routes we return not_found regardless of method. That's fine.\n\nOne more consideration — the task says \"Unsupported methods on a recognized route return status 405\". So HEAD/PUT/DELETE/anything → 405. My code: any non-GET/POST on collection → 405; any non-GET on detail → 405. ✓\n\nURL with only query, e.g. \"?decision=approve\" → pathname \"/\" → not_found. Fine.\n\nNow — response shape check: `respond` returns exactly `{status, headers, body}`. ✓ Fresh headers object each call. ✓\n\nNow the store file, final:\n\n```js\nconst REVIEW_FIELDS = [\"runId\", \"decision\", \"reviewer\", \"note\"];\n\nfunction defaultNow() {\n  return new Date().toISOString();\n}\n\nfunction isRecord(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"object\" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction copyReview(review) {\n  return {\n    runId: review.runId,\n    decision: review.decision,\n    reviewer: review.reviewer,\n    note: review.note,\n    createdAt: review.createdAt,\n    updatedAt: review.updatedAt,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction compareReviews(a, b) {\n  if (a.updatedAt > b.updatedAt) {\n    return -1;\n  }\n  if (a.updatedAt < b.updatedAt) {\n    return 1;\n  }\n  if (a.runId < b.runId) {\n    return -1;\n  }\n  if (a.runId > b.runId) {\n    return 1;\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\nexport function createReviewStore({ now } = {}) {\n  const clock = now === undefined ? defaultNow : now;\n  if (typeof clock !== \"function\") {\n    throw new TypeError(\"createReviewStore: now must be a function\");\n  }\n\n  const reviews = new Map();\n\n  function save(input) {\n    if (!isRecord(input)) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"save: review must be an object\");\n    }\n    for (const field of REVIEW_FIELDS) {\n      if (typeof input[field] !== \"string\") {\n        throw new TypeError(`save: review.${field} must be a string`);\n      }\n    }\n\n    const timestamp = clock();\n    if (typeof timestamp !== \"string\" || timestamp.length === 0) {\n      throw new TypeError(\"save: now must return a non-empty string\");\n    }\n\n    const existing = reviews.get(input.runId);\n    const created = existing === undefined;\n    const stored = {\n      runId: input.runId,\n      decision: input.decision,\n      reviewer: input.reviewer,\n      note: input.note,\n      createdAt: created ? timestamp : existing.createdAt,\n      updatedAt: timestamp,\n    };\n    reviews.set(input.runId, stored);\n\n    return { created, review: copyReview(stored) };\n  }\n\n  function get(runId) {\n    const stored = reviews.get(runId);\n    return stored === undefined ? null : copyReview(stored);\n  }\n\n  function list({ decision } = {}) {\n    const selected = [];\n    for (const review of reviews.values()) {\n      if (decision === undefined || review.decision === decision) {\n        selected.push(copyReview(review));\n      }\n    }\n    selected.sort(compareReviews);\n    return selected;\n  }\n\n  return { save, get, list };\n}\n```\n\nCheck against the committed test:\n- clock(\"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\", \"2026-08-23T11:00:00.000Z\") — save called twice, clock called once per save. ✓ first.created true, updated.created false, list length 1, createdAt preserved, updatedAt replaced. ✓\n\nEdge: `createReviewStore({ now: undefined })` — uses default. `createReviewStore()` — `now` undefined → default. ✓\n\nNow student-tests.mjs — write four tests. Let me make sure they're meaningful and don't duplicate the committed ones.\n\nAlso README.md.\n\nOne more check on student test (c): `handle({ method: \"GET\", url: 42 })` → url non-string → invalid_request. ✓ `handle(null)` → not a record → invalid_request. ✓\n\nAnd in test (c) I assert `Object.keys(after)` deep equals `[\"status\", \"headers\", \"body\"]` — order matters in deepEqual for arrays; my respond helper creates keys in that order. ✓\n\nAlso — the filtered-list ordering check: in test (a), all three saved at the same timestamp. Tie-break ascending runId: run-alpha, run-bravo, run-charlie. ✓ Then update run-bravo at a later time → run-bravo first, then run-alpha, run-charlie (tie at old timestamp). ✓\n\nFor the note-required check in test (b): updating run-alpha from approve to reject with note \"Missing tests\" — valid. ✓\n\nLet me also add an assertion in test (b) for the exact unknown-fields message: `\"Unknown fields: alpha, zeta\"`. I control the message format, so exact match is safe and stronger. But careful — if I later change the message the test breaks; that's fine, it's my own test asserting my own contract. The plan says \"one stable message such as `Unknown fields: a, z`\". I'll assert exact equality.\n\nAlso in test (d), page escaping — note that `decision: \"reject\"` etc are also escaped (no special chars, fine). Check:\n- `html.includes(\"<script>\")` → false. But careful: my page has no legitimate `<script>` tags. ✓\n- escaped message present: `&lt;script&gt;alert(&quot;msg&quot;)&lt;/script&gt;` ✓\n- `html.includes('onload=\"alert')` → false ✓\n- `html.includes(\"<b>1</b>\")` → false; `html.includes(\"&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;\")` → true ✓\n- `html.includes(\"<img\")` → false ✓\n- also verify the escaped reviewer appears: `&lt;img src=x onerror=&quot;alert(1)&quot;&gt;` ✓\n\nLet me write out the escape of `<img src=x onerror=\"alert(1)\">`:\n- `<` → `&lt;`\n- `img src=x onerror=` stays\n- `\"` → `&quot;`\n- `alert(1)` stays\n- `\"` → `&quot;`\n- `>` → `&gt;`\nResult: `&lt;img src=x onerror=&quot;alert(1)&quot;&gt;` ✓\n\nEscape of `\" onload=\"alert(1)`:\n- `\"` → `&quot;`, ` onload=` stays, `\"` → `&quot;`, `alert(1)` stays\nResult: `&quot; onload=&quot;alert(1)` ✓\n\nEscape of `run-x\"><script>alert(1)</script>`:\n`run-x&quot;&gt;&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;` ✓\n\nEscape of `<script>alert(\"msg\")</script>`:\n`&lt;script&gt;alert(&quot;msg&quot;)&lt;/script&gt;` ✓\n\nEscape of `<b>1</b>`: `&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;` ✓\n\nNow README.md content:\n\n```md\n# Run review queue fixture\n\nA dependency-free, in-memory review queue for benchmark runs. It provides a\nstore (`review-store.mjs`), a synchronous JSON-style API boundary\n(`review-api.mjs`), and a server-rendered HTML page (`review-page.mjs`).\n\n## Routes\n\n### `POST /api/reviews`\n\nSaves the current review for a run. One review is kept per `runId`; posting\nagain for the same run replaces it.\n\n- Body: JSON-style object with exactly `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, `note`.\n  Any additional field is reported as a sorted `body` field error.\n- All four values must be strings and are trimmed before validation/storage.\n- `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n- `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n- `reviewer` must be 2–40 characters after trimming.\n- `note` may be up to 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n  `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n- Returns `201 { review }` for a new run, `200 { review }` for an update.\n- Invalid input returns `400 { \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": {...} }`\n  listing every detected problem; nothing is saved.\n\n### `GET /api/reviews`\n\nReturns `{ reviews, summary }` sorted by newest `updatedAt` first (ties broken\nby lexicographically smaller `runId`). `summary` always counts every stored\nreview and has exactly `total`, `approve`, `reject`, and `needs-work`. An\noptional `?decision=` query filters only `reviews`; an invalid decision value\nreturns the standard validation error.\n\n### `GET /api/reviews/:runId`\n\nReturns `200 { review }` or `404 { \"error\": \"review_not_found\" }`.\n\n## Errors and headers\n\nEvery response has the shape `{ status, headers, body }` and includes\n`content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n\n- `400 { \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": {...} }` — invalid input.\n- `400 { \"error\": \"invalid_request\" }` — unusable request object or URL.\n- `404 { \"error\": \"not_found\" }` — unknown route.\n- `404 { \"error\": \"review_not_found\" }` — unknown run id.\n- `405 { \"error\": \"method_not_allowed\" }` — unsupported method on a recognized\n  route; includes an `allow` header (`GET, POST` on the collection, `GET` on a\n  detail route).\n\n## Storage limits\n\nThe store is process-local and not durable: it keeps data only in memory, so\nall reviews reset on process restart. It has no external dependencies.\n```\n\nThat covers the three routes, input/error behavior, and non-durability. \n\nAlso — \"If you modified any files/styles/structures/configurations/workflows/... mentioned in AGENTS.md files, you MUST update the corresponding AGENTS.md files\" — I'm not modifying anything mentioned in AGENTS.md; the fixture README update is within the task scope. The root AGENTS.md describes the project map; my changes don't alter the map. No AGENTS.md update needed.\n\nThe user instructions also mention \"always make sure to update the documentation going forward for all the work we will do\" — README.md update covers that within the allowed scope. And \"junit coverage for all the apps under java-apps\" — irrelevant here (no java-apps involved).\n\nNow write all five files. Let me also double-check the student test file — \"at least three meaningful node:test cases... no skips, todos, or placeholder assertions\". Four tests with real assertions. ✓\n\nOne more review of a subtle detail in the committed test:\n\n```js\nconst listed = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/api/reviews?decision=approve\" });\nassert.deepEqual(listed.body.summary, { total: 1, approve: 1, reject: 0, \"needs-work\": 0 });\n```\n\nMy summary object: `{ total: all.length, approve: 0, reject: 0, \"needs-work\": 0 }` — deepEqual with the expected — key order doesn't matter for deepEqual on objects. ✓\n\nAnd the first committed test expects `created.body.review` deepEqual to exactly the six-key object — my store returns exactly six keys. ✓\n\nAlso check the third committed test: `Object.keys(result.body.fields).sort()` equals `[\"note\", \"reviewer\", \"runId\"]`. My fields object for that input: runId error, reviewer error, note error; no body error (no unknown keys). Keys sorted → [\"note\", \"reviewer\", \"runId\"]. ✓ And `store.list()` deepEqual `[]` — nothing saved. ✓\n\nNow — decision check on `values.decision === \"reject\"` for the note-required rule uses the trimmed decision. In committed test 3, decision is \"reject\" (valid), note \"\" → note error. ✓\n\nLet me also think again about `handlePost` when body has unknown fields AND the known fields are all valid: fields.body set → 400, no save. The task says \"Accept only runId, decision, reviewer, and note; report sorted unknown field names as a body field error.\" ✓\n\nWhat about a body where `note` is missing entirely for an approve review? `typeof body.note !== \"string\"` → fields.note = \"note must be a string\". Hmm — is that right? The contract says \"A saved input has string fields runId, decision, reviewer, and note\" and \"Trim all four string values before validation\" — all four are required fields. So missing note → field error. ✓ Even for approve, note must be present (possibly empty string). The committed tests always pass note. OK.\n\nNow, about test (c) asserting `notAllowed.headers.allow === \"GET, POST\"`. ✓ matches my implementation.\n\nAlright — also think about whether `handle` should accept `request` as an instance of a class etc. isRecord covers object non-null non-array. ✓\n\nOne more potential hidden-test concern: `createReviewApi` with a store that has save/get/list as non-function properties (e.g., strings) → TypeError. ✓ With a function store that has the methods? `typeof store.save` would work on functions too since functions can have properties. My check `store === null || store === undefined || typeof store.save !== \"function\"...` — for a primitive like `42`, `store.save` is undefined → TypeError thrown. ✓ For a string store \"x\" — `\"x\".save` undefined → TypeError. ✓\n\nNow, write the files.\n\nAlso one more look at plan checklist item (d) for student tests: \"page escaping with `<script>` / `\\\" onload=` payloads in message, every summary value, and every review field\". I'll put payload in all four summary values? \"every summary entry\" — I'll use `<b>...</b>`-style payloads in all four summary values to be thorough. Then the summary numbers displayed escaped. Let me craft:\n\nsummary: { total: '<1>', approve: '\"2\"', reject: \"'3'\", \"needs-work\": '<img src=x>' } — then assert `html.includes(\"<1>\") === false`, `html.includes('\"2\"') === false`... wait `\"2\"` — would `\"2\"` appear anywhere else? The escaped version is `&quot;2&quot;`. But could a literal `\"2\"` appear in static HTML? No. But this is getting fragile. Simpler: use distinctive payloads like `<b>1</b>` etc. and check each escaped form appears and raw doesn't. Let me use payloads: total `<b>total</b>`, approve `<b>approve</b>`... hmm those words might appear elsewhere as text. Use clearly unique markers: `<i>s1</i>`, `<i>s2</i>`, `<i>s3</i>`, `<i>s4</i>`. Raw `<i>s1</i>` shouldn't appear; escaped `&lt;i&gt;s1&lt;/i&gt;` should. `<i` shouldn't appear at all in the doc → assert `html.includes(\"<i>\")` false... simpler to assert per-value escaped forms present and `<i>` absent overall. \n\nLet me now write everything.\n\nAlso note: the page test should include a legit review row to exercise rendering — my payload review covers that.\n\nOne more consideration for the escaping test: my page includes `aria-live=\"polite\"` — the escaped message `&lt;script&gt;...` sits inside that region. ✓\n\nAlso assert page still structurally fine with malicious data: contains `<caption>Saved run reviews</caption>`.\n\nNow write the files.\n\nFor student-tests.mjs, I need imports:\n\n```js\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { createReviewApi } from \"./review-api.mjs\";\nimport { renderReviewPage } from \"./review-page.mjs\";\nimport { createReviewStore } from \"./review-store.mjs\";\n```\n\nTest 1 (store ordering/filter/isolation):\n\n```js\ntest(\"store orders by newest update with runId tie-breaks, filters, and isolates state\", () => {\n  let current = \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\";\n  const store = createReviewStore({ now: () => current });\n\n  const draft = { runId: \"run-bravo\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"initial\" };\n  store.save(draft);\n  draft.note = \"mutated after save\";\n  store.save({ runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"reject\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"Missing tests\" });\n  store.save({ runId: \"run-charlie\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"\" });\n\n  // Caller-side mutation must not leak into stored state.\n  assert.equal(store.get(\"run-bravo\").note, \"initial\");\n\n  // Equal timestamps fall back to ascending runId order.\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    store.list().map((review) => review.runId),\n    [\"run-alpha\", \"run-bravo\", \"run-charlie\"],\n  );\n\n  current = \"2026-08-23T11:00:00.000Z\";\n  store.save({ runId: \"run-bravo\", decision: \"needs-work\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"Add coverage\" });\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    store.list().map((review) => review.runId),\n    [\"run-bravo\", \"run-alpha\", \"run-charlie\"],\n  );\n\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    store.list({ decision: \"approve\" }).map((review) => review.runId),\n    [\"run-charlie\"],\n  );\n\n  // Returned reviews and arrays are copies.\n  const listed = store.list();\n  listed[0].note = \"mutated copy\";\n  listed.pop();\n  assert.equal(store.get(\"run-bravo\").note, \"Add coverage\");\n  assert.equal(store.list().length, 3);\n  assert.equal(store.get(\"run-missing\"), null);\n});\n```\n\nWait — `store.save(draft)` with clock returning current (10:00). Then mutate draft.note. Then two more saves at same timestamp. get(\"run-bravo\").note === \"initial\" (inbound copy). ✓\n\nTie order: alpha, bravo, charlie ✓. Then update bravo at 11:00 → bravo first ✓. Filter approve → only charlie (alpha is reject, bravo now needs-work) ✓. Outbound isolation ✓. get missing → null ✓.\n\nTest 2 (store input validation + clock):\n\n```js\ntest(\"store rejects invalid input and bad clocks with TypeError\", () => {\n  assert.throws(() => createReviewStore({ now: \"not a function\" }), TypeError);\n\n  const store = createReviewStore({ now: () => \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\" });\n  assert.throws(() => store.save(null), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => store.save([\"run-alpha\"]), TypeError);\n  assert.throws(() => store.save({ runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: 42 }), TypeError);\n  assert.deepEqual(store.list(), []);\n\n  let ticks = 0;\n  const flaky = createReviewStore({\n    now: () => {\n      ticks += 1;\n      return ticks === 1 ? \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\" : \"\";\n    },\n  });\n  flaky.save({ runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"\" });\n  assert.throws(() => flaky.save({ runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"reject\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"x\" }), TypeError);\n\n  // The failed update must not mutate the stored review.\n  assert.equal(flaky.get(\"run-alpha\").decision, \"approve\");\n  assert.equal(flaky.get(\"run-alpha\").updatedAt, \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\");\n});\n```\n\nTest 3 (API lifecycle + validation):\n\n```js\ntest(\"api validates posts, reports sorted unknown fields, and never stores invalid data\", () => {\n  let current = \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\";\n  const store = createReviewStore({ now: () => current });\n  const handle = createReviewApi(store);\n\n  assert.throws(() => createReviewApi({ save() {} }), TypeError);\n\n  const created = handle({\n    method: \"POST\",\n    url: \"/api/reviews\",\n    body: { runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"\" },\n  });\n  assert.equal(created.status, 201);\n\n  current = \"2026-08-23T11:00:00.000Z\";\n  const updated = handle({\n    method: \"POST\",\n    url: \"/api/reviews\",\n    body: { runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"reject\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"Missing tests\" },\n  });\n  assert.equal(updated.status, 200);\n  assert.equal(updated.body.review.createdAt, \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\");\n  assert.equal(updated.body.review.updatedAt, \"2026-08-23T11:00:00.000Z\");\n  assert.equal(updated.body.review.decision, \"reject\");\n\n  const unknown = handle({\n    method: \"POST\",\n    url: \"/api/reviews\",\n    body: { runId: \"run-beta\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"\", zeta: 1, alpha: 2 },\n  });\n  assert.equal(unknown.status, 400);\n  assert.equal(unknown.body.fields.body, \"Unknown fields: alpha, zeta\");\n  assert.equal(store.get(\"run-beta\"), null);\n\n  const missingBody = handle({ method: \"POST\", url: \"/api/reviews\" });\n  assert.equal(missingBody.status, 400);\n  assert.equal(missingBody.body.error, \"validation_failed\");\n  assert.equal(typeof missingBody.body.fields.body, \"string\");\n\n  const invalid = handle({\n    method: \"POST\",\n    url: \"/api/reviews\",\n    body: { runId: \"run-gamma\", decision: \"needs-work\", reviewer: \"A\", note: \"\" },\n  });\n  assert.equal(invalid.status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(invalid.body.fields).sort(), [\"note\", \"reviewer\"]);\n  assert.deepEqual(store.list().map((review) => review.runId), [\"run-alpha\"]);\n});\n```\n\nWait: runId \"run-gamma\" matches pattern ✓, decision needs-work valid, reviewer \"A\" too short → error, note empty + needs-work → error. Fields: note, reviewer. ✓ Store still only has run-alpha. ✓\n\nTest 4 (API routing/errors + summary):\n\n```js\ntest(\"api routes reads, filters, and errors without leaking headers\", () => {\n  const store = createReviewStore({ now: () => \"2026-08-23T12:00:00.000Z\" });\n  const handle = createReviewApi(store);\n  handle({ method: \"POST\", url: \"/api/reviews\", body: { runId: \"run-alpha\", decision: \"approve\", reviewer: \"Ada\", note: \"\" } });\n  handle({ method: \"POST\", url: \"/api/reviews\", body: { runId: \"run-beta\", decision: \"reject\", reviewer: \"Bob\", note: \"Flaky\" } });\n\n  const filtered = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/api/reviews?decision=reject\" });\n  assert.equal(filtered.status, 200);\n  assert.deepEqual(filtered.body.reviews.map((review) => review.runId), [\"run-beta\"]);\n  // Summary stays global even when reviews are filtered.\n  assert.deepEqual(filtered.body.summary, { total: 2, approve: 1, reject: 1, \"needs-work\": 0 });\n\n  const badFilter = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/api/reviews?decision=mixed\" });\n  assert.equal(badFilter.status, 400);\n  assert.equal(badFilter.body.error, \"validation_failed\");\n\n  const detail = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/api/reviews/run-alpha\" });\n  assert.equal(detail.status, 200);\n  assert.equal(detail.body.review.runId, \"run-alpha\");\n\n  const missing = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/api/reviews/run-missing\" });\n  assert.equal(missing.status, 404);\n  assert.deepEqual(missing.body, { error: \"review_not_found\" });\n\n  const collectionMethod = handle({ method: \"DELETE\", url: \"/api/reviews\" });\n  assert.equal(collectionMethod.status, 405);\n  assert.equal(collectionMethod.headers.allow, \"GET, POST\");\n\n  const detailMethod = handle({ method: \"POST\", url: \"/api/reviews/run-alpha\" });\n  assert.equal(detailMethod.status, 405);\n  assert.deepEqual(detailMethod.body, { error: \"method_not_allowed\" });\n  assert.equal(detailMethod.headers.allow, \"GET\");\n\n  // The 405 allow header must not leak into later responses.\n  const after = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/api/reviews/run-alpha\" });\n  assert.equal(\"allow\" in after.headers, false);\n  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(after), [\"status\", \"headers\", \"body\"]);\n\n  const unknown = handle({ method: \"GET\", url: \"/somewhere/else\" });\n  assert.equal(unknown.status, 404);\n  assert.deepEqual(unknown.body, { error: \"not_found\" });\n\n  assert.equal(handle(null).status, 400);\n  assert.deepEqual(handle(null).body, { error: \"invalid_request\" });\n  assert.deepEqual(handle({ method: \"GET\", url: 42 }).body, { error: \"invalid_request\" });\n});\n```\n\nHmm — `Object.keys(after)` order: my respond returns object literal `{ status, headers, body }` — insertion order preserved. ✓\n\nTest 5 (page escaping):\n\n```js\ntest(\"page escapes injected markup in the message, summary, and review fields\", () => {\n  const html = renderReviewPage({\n    reviews: [\n      {\n        runId: 'run-x\"><script>alert(1)</script>',\n        decision: \"reject\",\n        reviewer: '<img src=x onerror=\"alert(1)\">',\n        note: '\" onload=\"alert(1)',\n        createdAt: \"2026-08-23T10:00:00.000Z\",\n        updatedAt: \"2026-08-23T11:00:00.000Z\",\n      },\n    ],\n    summary: { total: \"<i>s1</i>\", approve: \"<i>s2</i>\", reject: \"<i>s3</i>\", \"needs-work\": \"<i>s4</i>\" },\n    message: '<script>alert(\"msg\")</script>',\n  });\n\n  assert.equal(html.includes(\"<script>\"), false);\n  assert.equal(html.includes(\"<img\"), false);\n  assert.equal(html.includes(\"<i>\"), false);\n  assert.equal(html.includes('onload=\"alert'), false);\n  assert.equal(html.includes('onerror=\"alert'), false);\n\n  assert.ok(html.includes(\"&lt;script&gt;alert(&quot;msg&quot;)&lt;/script&gt;\"));\n  assert.ok(html.includes(\"run-x&quot;&gt;&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;\"));\n  assert.ok(html.includes(\"&lt;img src=x onerror=&quot;alert(1)&quot;&gt;\"));\n  assert.ok(html.includes(\"&quot; onload=&quot;alert(1)\"));\n  for (const marker of [\"s1\", \"s2\", \"s3\", \"s4\"]) {\n    assert.ok(html.includes(`&lt;i&gt;${marker}&lt;/i&gt;`));\n  }\n\n  // The document structure stays intact despite hostile data.\n  assert.ok(html.startsWith(\"<!DOCTYPE html>\"));\n  assert.ok(html.includes('<caption>Saved run reviews</caption>'));\n  assert.ok(html.includes('aria-live=\"polite\"'));\n});\n```\n\nCheck `html.includes('onerror=\"alert')` — escaped reviewer: `&lt;img src=x onerror=&quot;alert(1)&quot;&gt;` — contains `onerror=&quot;alert` not `onerror=\"alert`. ✓ And `onload=\"alert` → escaped is `onload=&quot;alert` ✓.\n\nCareful: does the string `<img` appear anywhere in static page HTML? No. `<script>`? No. `<i>`? No — my page uses no `<i>` elements. ✓\n\nWait — one more check on `html.startsWith(\"<!DOCTYPE html>\")` — my template starts with `<!DOCTYPE html>` exactly (no leading newline). In my template literal, I write `return `<!DOCTYPE html>...` — starts immediately. ✓\n\nNow — do all 5 student tests pass with my implementation? Let me trace through mentally once more after writing.\n\nAlso, subtle: in test 3, `assert.throws(() => createReviewApi({ save() {} }), TypeError)` — store missing get/list → TypeError ✓.\n\nAnd the `missingBody` case: `handle({ method: \"POST\", url: \"/api/reviews\" })` — request.body undefined → not a record → validationFailed({ body: ... }) — status 400, error validation_failed, fields.body a string ✓.\n\nNow let me also double check `list({ decision } = {})` when called with no args → decision undefined → all. When called `store.list()` in committed test ✓.\n\nAlso the committed test calls `store.list()` — returns [] deepEqual [] when empty ✓.\n\nAlright — also consider: in `handleReviewRequest`, `request.body` access — if request is a record, fine.\n\nOne thing: for `handlePost`, what if `trimmed.decision` is undefined (non-string decision) but note is empty? Note-required check: `trimmed.decision === \"reject\" || ...` → undefined !== those → no note-required error. But fields.decision already has \"must be a string\". OK.\n\nWhat if decision is invalid string \"maybe\" and note empty? decision error only. Fine — \"Report all detected field problems\". Not reporting note-required for an unknown decision is correct behavior since the rule is conditional on reject/needs-work.\n\nEdge: note exactly 240 chars → OK. 241 → error. Reviewer exactly 2 and exactly 40 → OK.\n\nrunId pattern: `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$` — \"run-alpha\" ✓. Total length: 4 + 1 + 2..63 = 7..68 chars.\n\nNow, final check on page template — the committed test regex `/<main>/`: my `<main>` has no attributes ✓.\n\nLabels: `<label for=\"run-id\">Run ID</label>` exact ✓. Also labels for decision/reviewer/note.\n\nForm method=\"post\" action=\"/api/reviews\" ✓.\n\nNote-required description ✓ (note-help paragraph + aria-describedby).\n\nSummary values: rendered in `<ul>` as `<li><strong>Total reviews:</strong> 0</li>` etc. \"Show all four summary values\" ✓.\n\nTable: caption, five th with scope=\"col\", rows or empty state ✓.\n\nEverything escaped ✓.\n\nI think the implementation is solid. Let me write the files now.\n\nOne more thought on `respond` with `extraHeaders` — I'll default it to `{}` for clarity: `function respond(status, body, extraHeaders = {})`.\n\nAlso — in `handleReviewRequest`, empty method string check: `method.length === 0` → invalid_request. Hmm, actually should whitespace-only or empty method be 405 on a recognized route instead? The task: \"An unusable request object or URL returns status 400\" — an empty method makes the request unusable. I'll include the check. It won't affect any visible test.\n\nWriting files now. After that, run the allowed test command.\n\nFor the README, keep it concise but complete.\n\nAlso, AGENTS.md note: \"If you modified any files/styles/structures/configurations/workflows/... mentioned in AGENTS.md files, you MUST update the corresponding AGENTS.md files\" — the fixture README is not mentioned in AGENTS.md. The project map mentions `benchmark/tasks/` etc. but my changes don't modify the map structure. No AGENTS.md change needed.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_02fc705f7001wg7R2cnT0b1wr9","sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","messageID":"msg_02fc66b6c001bYWPrkXHXNZnol"}}
