{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787507989142,"sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"bash:19","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node --test benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs","workdir":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout"},"output":"✔ stores one current review per run and preserves creation time (0.592333ms)\n✔ creates, normalizes, lists, and filters reviews through the API (0.86ms)\n✔ returns field errors instead of saving an invalid decision (0.106ms)\n✔ renders a labeled form, summary, table, and empty state (0.189583ms)\n✔ store orders by newest update with runId tie-breaks, filters, and isolates state (1.134375ms)\n✔ store rejects invalid input and unusable clocks with TypeError (0.210834ms)\n✔ api validates posts, reports sorted unknown fields, and never stores invalid data (0.275125ms)\n✔ api routes reads and errors, keeps summaries global, and never leaks headers (0.377166ms)\n✔ page escapes injected markup in the message, summary, and review fields (0.209292ms)\nℹ tests 9\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 9\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 66.580125\n","metadata":{"output":"✔ stores one current review per run and preserves creation time (0.592333ms)\n✔ creates, normalizes, lists, and filters reviews through the API (0.86ms)\n✔ returns field errors instead of saving an invalid decision (0.106ms)\n✔ renders a labeled form, summary, table, and empty state (0.189583ms)\n✔ store orders by newest update with runId tie-breaks, filters, and isolates state (1.134375ms)\n✔ store rejects invalid input and unusable clocks with TypeError (0.210834ms)\n✔ api validates posts, reports sorted unknown fields, and never stores invalid data (0.275125ms)\n✔ api routes reads and errors, keeps summaries global, and never leaks headers (0.377166ms)\n✔ page escapes injected markup in the message, summary, and review fields (0.209292ms)\nℹ tests 9\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 9\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 66.580125\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"node --test benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs","time":{"start":1787507989139,"end":1787507989141}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now run the verification command — the only allowed bash command.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_02fc759f4001W5YNDD76sqdCVm","sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","messageID":"msg_02fc75443001EPhY5hi09vB88C"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1787507989158,"sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","part":{"id":"prt_02fc75aa5001pcaWq2ClAaQKyl","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"89a13d65b11cf9ccd9dc428e1b704e8cc50516e8","messageID":"msg_02fc75443001EPhY5hi09vB88C","sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":42213,"input":78,"output":134,"reasoning":17,"cache":{"write":0,"read":41984}},"cost":0.0150942}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1787507990638,"sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","part":{"id":"prt_02fc76063001xCP507KtWsQVsB","messageID":"msg_02fc75aba001c6G1tvAxiYYUT0","sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","snapshot":"89a13d65b11cf9ccd9dc428e1b704e8cc50516e8","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1787507995203,"sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","part":{"id":"prt_02fc7646f001WshN9H6rug5Bxp","messageID":"msg_02fc75aba001c6G1tvAxiYYUT0","sessionID":"ses_fd03a4315ffec31s0GggcSnBoE","type":"text","text":"All 9 tests pass (4 committed + 5 added). Only the five allowed files were modified.\n\n## Design summary\n\n**`review-store.mjs`** — `createReviewStore({ now } = {})` wraps a private `Map` keyed by `runId`. It throws `TypeError` for a non-function `now`, a non-object/array input, or non-string fields. `save` validates input fully *before* calling `now()` exactly once, and throws `TypeError` on a non-empty-string violation without mutating the map (updates stay atomic). Inserts share one timestamp for `createdAt`/`updatedAt`; updates preserve `createdAt`. Stored reviews contain exactly the six contract keys, and every input is copied in and every result copied out, so neither caller-side nor returned-value mutation can leak into stored state. `list` sorts with `<`/`>` (locale-independent): `updatedAt` descending, `runId` ascending on ties.\n\n**`review-api.mjs`** — `createReviewApi(store)` validates the store has callable `save`/`get`/`list` (else `TypeError`) and returns the `handleReviewRequest` function directly. One `respond` helper builds a fresh `{ status, headers, body }` per call, so a 405's `allow` header can never poison later responses. POST accumulates *all* field problems (sorted unknown-field names as a `body` error, type errors, then trimmed format/length/note-required checks) and never calls `save` on invalid data; 201 insert / 200 update. GET collection computes a global summary from one unfiltered `list()` and filters only `reviews`; invalid `?decision=` (including empty) → standard validation error. Detail route decodes one non-empty segment with a `try/catch` guard. Malformed request objects/URLs → `invalid_request`; recognized routes with wrong methods → 405 with `allow` (`GET, POST` / `GET`); everything else → `not_found`.\n\n**`review-page.mjs`** — complete HTML document with an attribute-free `<main>`, one `<h1>`, explanation, all four escaped summary values, a static `aria-live=\"polite\"` status region, a POST form with exact labels (`<label for=\"run-id\">Run ID</label>` etc.) and note-required guidance linked via `aria-describedby`, and a table with `<caption>Saved run reviews</caption>`, five `scope=\"col\"` headers, and a `colspan=\"5\"` `No reviews yet.` empty state. Every dynamic value passes through an escaper covering `& < > \" '`, and caller data never appears in tag or attribute positions.\n\n## Tests added (5, no skips/todos)\n\n1. Store tie-break ordering, decision filtering, and copy isolation in **both** directions (mutated input after `save`, mutated `list` results).\n2. Store `TypeError` paths: non-function clock, null/array input, non-string field, empty-string clock result — verifying a failed update leaves stored state untouched.\n3. API update flow (200, preserved `createdAt`), exact sorted unknown-field message (`Unknown fields: alpha, zeta`), missing-body error, and confirmation invalid posts never reach the store.\n4. API routing: global summary under a filter, invalid filter, detail 404, both 405 `allow` values, no `allow` leakage into the next response, exact response key shape, unknown-route 404, and `invalid_request` for null/numeric-URL requests.\n5. Page escaping with `<script>`, `<img onerror>`, and attribute-injection payloads in the message, all four summary values, and all review fields — asserting raw markup is absent and escaped forms are present.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nnode --test benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/review-queue.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/student-tests.mjs\n→ tests 9, pass 9, fail 0\n```\n\n## Remaining concern\n\nThe contract references a private hidden suite that cannot be inspected or executed here. Undocumented edges — exact field-error message wording, tolerance of a trailing slash on `/api/reviews/`, and percent-decoding of detail ids — follow the plan-reviewed interpretation of the written contract, but only the visible suite's behavior is confirmed.","time":{"start":1787507991663,"end":1787507995200}}}
